# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Chain two paid mana abilities after one ordinary source, then spend the remaining mana on a spell.
# Forcing: Mountain cannot cast Manalith alone, and neither Signet can activate without mana from an earlier source.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no battlefield or hand, so it makes no decisions.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = Mountain funds both Signets in sequence and Manalith resolves.
#   LOSE = the spell is not cast before the one-turn deadline.
#   TIMEOUT = activation, payment, or resolution stops advancing.
# Card roles:
#   Mountain — supplies the first activation cost.
#   Rakdos Signet — produces the seed for the second paid source and one mana for the spell.
#   Gruul Signet — produces the remaining two mana for the spell.
#   Manalith — observable three-mana consumer of the chained payment.
# Protocol path: cast action, nested mana payments, source taps, spell payment, and permanent resolution.

[metadata]
Name:Chained Paid Mana Filter
Goal:Play the Specified Permanent
Targets:Manalith
Turns:1
Difficulty:Easy
Description:Chain two Signets from one Mountain to cast Manalith.

